and i was like all swollen underneath  the makeup  and it was turns out a trip to hawkins  isn't all sunshine and daisies  both on screen and behind the scenes  stranger things has had their fair share  of goriness and horror over the past  three seasons and while we may think  it looked epic on screen it's at the  expense of the cast  suffering through just as many hours in  the makeup department  as they do on set it's time to find out  just what would make the stranger things  cast  want to trade a day in prosthetics for a  trip to the upside down  instead i've been waiting to meet this  king steve everybody's been telling me  so much about both billy hargrove and  daker montgomery were put through the  ringer in season three  just in different ways with the mind  flayer on the loose and getting mixed up  with billy it resulted in plenty of  wounds  wounds that were all created by the  makeup and special effects department  there was no cgi or vfx for this  character  daker spent hours on end in the makeup  chair before heading to set  each day and when billy was at his worst  daker was sporting  33 prosthetics at once 33.  between him and his stunt double the  makeup team had to create and apply 99  prosthetics in one day  he was wearing so much glue that during  one of his lunch breaks his arm  prosthetics got stuck to the tablecloth  what made things even worse is millie  bobby brown's knee injury  actually caused the filming of daker  scenes to be pushed up with barely any  notice  the makeup department head amy l  forsythe said  i got a call during the hiatus giving me  a heads up about doing the post sauna  scene with billy on the stairwell  getting his wounds nursed the day  after we were to get back from hiatus i  hadn't even seen a preview for the sauna  fight so i didn't know how he was  getting hurt or where his wounds might  be  i gotta warn you again in your band for  life the duffer brothers were super  adamant about including as many  practical effects as they could in  stranger things  which means season one barely required  any digital visual effects  including the demogorgon the demogorgon  was actually just one big prosthetic  suit that was worn by actor mark steger  however opting for practical effects  came with some pretty big challenges for  mark  he had to perform some intense stunts in  the suit that he couldn't properly hear  or see in  but he did say that it helped him  remember why he loved film  in the later seasons the duffer brothers  eventually decided to move on to more of  a cgi route  let's just say things got a little too  gooey  it's crazy this is crazy this is crazy  daker loved being able to embrace billy  by adding on his  bad boy characteristics like his tattoo  and scar  however it was at the expense of  spending more time in the makeup chair  after a full day of filming daker would  endure another two  hours removing the prosthetics from his  body including the prosthetics he needed  to cover his facial hair  shadow he wore the prosthetic so much  that at one point he noticed his body  hair wasn't even growing back anymore  every day when you spend like two hours  getting them off like i remember there  was a big cut and scar  right here you can see i've got no hair  on my arm there because it's just been  months and months of shaving right in  that spot  it shouldn't have looked for me as much  as we all love steve harrington now  there was a time where him getting beat  up wasn't something we felt bad about  but you might feel bad for joe kiri when  you hear what he had to go through while  wearing these prosthetics  not only was joe sick on the day they  shot these scenes but he had to have  menthol blown in his eyes to achieve the  desired effects  ouch to be specific amy shared that his  prosthetics included a swollen jaw lump  cut split lip  and a mixture of cotton and dried blood  she shared her process on instagram and  even called joe  a trooper ahoy ladies i didn't see you  there  will's possession scene took a major  toll on noah schnapp  both mentally and physically not only  did he have to put himself in a dark  place but his costume consisted of black  contacts that made his eyes burn  his costume was also not designed for  the weather although it may have looked  like it was warm on screen  noah explains it was filmed in the  middle of winter there was just so much  going on  the heaters didn't actually heat up it  wasn't really hot  it was actually really cold because it  was winter  the cherry on top of it all was that  noah was so overworked and tired he woke  up the next day with  no voice i was screaming the whole night  and the next morning i woke up and my  voice had disappeared  movie makeup doesn't always mean gory  wounds and scars  sometimes the actors have a difficult  time wearing foundation  heaps of it nancy never really found  herself in a situation that led to an  injury but she did spend hours each day  in the makeup chair  it may not seem like it but natalie dyer  says she wore  so much makeup on set that she began  suffering from acne  the only solution was for her to amp up  her skincare game to prevent it from  getting any worse  we ask for forgiveness not permission  what the audience doesn't realize is  that prosthetics can sometimes minimize  an actor's senses  in this intense shower scene that daker  had to film he was so  physically involved that he was actually  injured without even realizing  he was only able to see the scrapes and  bruises that he accumulated on his body  after taking off the prosthetics he was  wearing just listen to him explain his  experience  i was covered head to toe in cuts and  bruises and i took all the skin off the  top of my toes and  one of stranger things goriest scenes  had to be when a mind flayer  literally hatches from eleven's leg  while the mind flayer in this scene was  digitally added  in post-production everything else about  the wound was done using makeup and  prosthetics  millie had the benefit of using a  prosthetic leg instead of her own  however it was still pretty gross to  work with but not gross enough to stop  her from taking an instagram selfie with  it it took  months of research from the makeup  department in order to make the leg and  wound look as realistic as possible  and it's safe to say they did a duffer  brother approved job  i could do it who knew how versatile lip  gloss could be  billy's flayed look was achieved by  applying layers and layers of mac  clear lip gloss all in all he had to  wear a layer of lip gloss  a layer of dirt and mud and then another  layer of lip gloss to seal it all  together  as you can imagine wearing lip gloss  wasn't the most comfortable experience  but daker said it worked better in the  scene that he wasn't constantly having  to be sprayed with water  all day to achieve the wet look just  look how big that lip gloss jar  is one of the things we've gathered from  going behind the scenes of stranger  things  is that millie bobby brown gives her all  into her character 11.  no matter the circumstances  filming her scenes in the voyage shook  her to her core literally  her wardrobe was not cut out for how  cold it was on set that day  especially because she was constantly  working with water the stranger things  art director said  the one thing you are missing is that it  was freezing cold on stage that day we  shot this  and millie was a real trooper splashing  around in the cold water  sfx tried to heat it but it was too  shallow to retain  any heat don't be afraid don't be afraid  when you think about who the duffer  brothers were inspired by steven  spielberg  stephen king and john carpenter it's no  surprise they went down the practical  effects route even if it was  uncomfortable for the stranger things  cast at times  in addition to all the prosthetics and  makeup they even used practical effects  to create a lot of the upside down set  and brutal battle scenes like bob's  demise  did we mention that will's body double  was so realistically made by the makeup  department that they were able to pull  off the ultimate prank on noah schnapp's  mom  the question is what's worse wearing  prosthetics and makeup  or fighting demogorgons after hearing  about how barb's actress shannon purser  had to eat  baby food for her pool scene and bob's  actor shawn aston had to continuously  put fake blood in his mouth  we are going with demogorgons all jokes  aside the stranger things cast truly  does give their all  into every single episode they film and  these behind the scenes moments spell it  out perfectly  which actor do you think had it worse  when it came to special effects  let us know below thanks for watching
 

